>> title: No-Marinade Chicken Fajita
>> servings: 5
>> source: https://www.spendwithpennies.com/easy-chicken-fajitas

Cut @onion{1%medium}(into slivers) & slice @bell peppers{3}(red, yellow, green or orange).

In a separate bowl, combine @olive oil{1%tbsp}, juice of @lime{1}(fresh), and juice of @lime{}(remaining), @chili powder{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/2%tsp}, @onion powder{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, @cumin{1/2%tsp} and @salt{1/2%tsp}. Cut @chicken breasts{3}(boneless skinless) into strips and toss with the spice mixture.

Preheat @olive oil{1%tbsp} over medium high. Add half of the chicken and cook until just cooked, about ~{3-5%minutes}. Remove from the pan and set aside. Repeat with remaining chicken.

Set chicken aside and add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to the pan. Cook onions for ~{2%minutes}. Add in sliced peppers and season with remaining @salt{1/4%tsp}. Toss and cook for an additional ~{2%minutes} or just until hot. Add chicken back to the pan and stir to combine.

Squeeze additional @lime{}(juice) overtop and serve over tortillas.